## Your rights

You can:
- **See** the data we hold about you, and get a copy (**download your data**)
- **Correct** it if it's wrong
- **Delete** it (**delete your account**)
- **Withdraw consent** you gave earlier, at any time
{% if eu %}
- **Object** to processing based on our legitimate interests, and ask us to **restrict** processing
- **Complain** to your data protection authority (in the UK, the ICO)
{% endif %}
{% if california %}
- **California residents:** know what we collect, delete it, correct it, opt out of its sale or sharing, and limit use of sensitive data. We won't treat you differently for using these rights. We honor the Global Privacy Control signal as an opt-out.
{% endif %}

To use these rights, use your account settings or email {{ contact_email }}. We reply within {% if eu %}one month{% else %}45 days{% endif %} and may need to confirm your identity first.

## Children

{% if minors == "under13" %}
Children under 13 may only use the service with a parent's verified consent. Parents can review or delete their child's data by emailing {{ contact_email }}.
{% else %}
The service isn't meant for anyone under {{ min_age }}. If you think a child has given us data, email {{ contact_email }} and we'll delete it.
{% endif %}

## Security

We protect your data with encryption in transit, access controls and hashed passwords. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you, we'll tell you as the law requires.

{% if eu %}
## International transfers

Some of our providers are outside the EU/UK. Where they are, we rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or Standard Contractual Clauses.
{% endif %}

## Changes

If we change this policy, we'll update the date above and tell you by email or in the app before important changes take effect.
